Vacancy Listing Dates 20/07/2026 to 17/08/2026
Please Quote Reference Number 17715
- Immediate start
- Competitive remuneration package available
- Join the team at JA Engineering in Parkhurst

JAE is a mechanical engineering business that specialises in the manufacturing and refurbishment of coal mining machines and equipment, in accordance with OEM (original equipment manufacturer) specifications and government legislations.

JAE is searching for an Engineering Manager to join their team who will report to the Operations Manager.

These tasks include:
- Actively work with the team to drive improvement initiatives, quantify benefits and track performance;
- Determine, implement and monitor engineering strategies, policies and plans;
- Ensure conformity with specifications and plans, and with laws, regulations and safety standards;
- Establish project / job schedules to manage workflow and budgets;
- Instil a growth and learning mind-set within the Engineering Department to increase overall strength;
- Interpret drawings, specifications and plans to provide advice on engineering methods and procedures to achieve manufacturing requirements;
- Liaise with senior management regarding engineering aspects of new product design;
- Maintain and ensure prescribed engineering standards of quality, cost, safety, timeliness and performance are observed;
- Oversee maintenance requirements to optimise efficiency;
- Participate in research and development projects, establishing processes to identify opportunities and improvements on delivering innovative products.

To be considered you will need a relevant degree or higher with two years minimum relevant employment experience or at least five years of relevant employment experience to substitute for the formal qualification.

This is a full time role with an immediate start available. Competitive remuneration package available to the successful candidate.

APPLY NOW through our online application form - https://www.netyourjob.com.au/jobs/17715.php

Romeo’s Best Vineyards Pty Ltd is one of Australia’s largest privately owned table grape producers. Romeo’s Best Farms are located in prime growing areas across the East Coast and Central Australia, including Mutchilba, Mareeba, Emerald, and St George in Queensland, as well as Robinvale in Victoria. The business aims to produce quality Australian table grapes all year round.

We are seeking a full-time and fully qualified accountant to join our finance team based in Robinvale VIC 3549. In this role, the successful applicant will take ownership of our daily financial functions and elevate our strategic reporting. The applicant should have a relevant bachelor’s degree in accounting or finance.

Salary is $79,499 per annum plus super.

The Accountant at Romeo’s Best Farms will be responsible for the following tasks:
• Assisting in formulating and implementing budgetary controls and accounting policies tailored to agricultural operations;
• Preparing and presenting accurate financial statements for review by the Board of Directors, management and relevant statutory bodies;
• Providing assurance about the accuracy of information contained in financial reports and their compliance with statutory requirements;
• Preparing and lodging taxation returns for the business;
• Maintaining, reviewing and strengthening internal control systems to protect assets and maintain data integrity across all business locations;
• Examining operating costs, seasonal vineyard inputs, and organisation expenditure to optimise profit margins;
• Evaluating cash flow requirements and appraising financial risks for capital investment projects;
• Providing expert financial and taxation advice regarding business structures, future expansion plans and operational efficiencies;
• Maintaining and optimising current accounting systems, and advising on the selection and integration of modern, agricultural or inventory-based accounting software;
• Liaising with financial institutions and brokers to establish, monitor and optimise funds management and seasonal finance arrangements;
• Conducting targeted financial investigations, managing external audits, and advising on complex matters including capital financing, business restructuring, tax strategy, or risk management.

Adelaide SA, Perth WA, North West QLD, and NSW, Full Time, Trades & Services
Vacancy Listing Dates 28/07/2026 to 25/08/2026
Please Quote Reference Number 17765
- Skilled Fitters, Formwork Carpenters, and Mining Engineer wanted
- Full time opportunities
- Join the Redpath Australia team in various locations

At Redpath Australia Pty Ltd, we have the expertise, track record and qualifications to support any scope of work, even in the most remote parts of the world. Our projects are started well on time and are executed with the highest safety standards and exceptional workmanship. We serve our international client base from our offices and facilities across the globe.

We currently have vacancies available in these locations:
- Formwork Carpenter - Perth based and will work at WA mine sites
- Fitter - Dugald Mine, North West QLD
- Fitter - Olympic Dam, South Australia (Adelaide region)
- Mining Engineer - Appin Mine, Menangle NSW

We are currently seeking experienced Fitters to join our team full time in Dugald Mine, North West QLD and Olympic Dam, South Australia (Adelaide region).

The Fitter is responsible for carrying out general mechanical work including repairs, attending breakdowns and service work in a workshop and underground environment to heavy mobile and fixed plant and equipment.

Duties & Responsibilities:
- in accordance with Redpath and Client's Management Systems, perform the works as directed, with particular emphasis on Safety, Efficiency and Quality;
- ensure compliance with Redpath and the Client's Management Systems and the relevant statutory regulations;
- present for work satisfying the requirements of Redpath and the Client's "fitness for work standards";
- strict adherence to the Redpath's Philosophy, Guidelines for Success, Code of Conduct and Cardinal Rules;
- carry out scheduled maintenance and breakdown repairs to a fleet of large mobile plant;
- fault finding repairing and/or replacing components as required;
- maintain plant and equipment, ensuring compliance with regulations and site requirements;
- keep a clean & tidy workshop;
- file documents daily;
- investigate ICAM accidents as required;
- fill out and sign maintenance worksheets daily;
- conduct oil sampling as required;
- attend and contribute to pre-start meetings, toolbox talks, safety meetings, roster change and shift change meetings when required;
- complete all pre start checks prior to use of equipment;
- conduct TTTC's and THA's as required;
- report immediately any incidents, accidents or near misses;
- any other duties that Redpath may direct you to perform, which you are capable of performing;
- only perform tasks you are trained in, competent in and authorised to perform the tasks.

Required Skills, Knowledge, Qualifications:
- heavy duty diesel fitter/mechanic trade qualification;
- proven experience with underground hard rock mobile plant equipment
- auto electrical knowledge;
- valid manual drivers licence;
- current CPR certificate (HLTCPR201A - Perform CPR);
- strong fault finding & diagnostic skills;
- strong planning and organising skills to schedule and complete tasks;
- the ability to work well with others in a team environment as well as work unsupervised;
- good verbal and written communication skills;
- able to follow written and verbal instructions accurately and complete assigned tasks safely;
- a safety approach upholding Redpath's principle of Safety - First, Last and Always;
- a drive for continuous improvement and contribute to an environment of innovation;
- able to prioritise and schedule tasks according to changing priorities.

We are also seeking a Formwork Carpenter to also join our team based in Perth, with travel required within WA to support our operations at mine sites.

Applicants for these roles will also need 1+ year of experience and to hold a relevant trade qualification.

A pay of $60-80 per hour will be offered the the successful candidates for the Fitter and Formwork Carpenter roles.

We also require a Mining Engineer to join our team

Key Responsibilities:
- Ensure all work is carried out safely and in line with company procedures, legislation, and quality standards.
- Assist with planning, coordinating, and supervising daily and weekly shaft construction activities to achieve production targets.
- Monitor shaft construction progress, ground support installation, and concrete lining to ensure compliance with engineering and geotechnical specifications.
- Prepare, review, and optimise drill and blast plans, while supervising blasting activities and managing blast performance.
- Collect, analyse, and report production, quality, and performance data, ensuring accurate project documentation and reporting.
- Inspect shaft sinking installations and maintain quality assurance, QA/QC processes, and blasting equipment.
- Participate in safety meetings, risk assessments, and project planning activities.
- Mentor and support operational personnel, contributing to training, development, and ongoing improvement initiatives.
- Undertake Shaft Supervisor responsibilities as required as part of ongoing development.

Applicants for this role need to hold a relevant qualification and have at least 1 year of experience in a similar role. The successful applicant will be offered $150,000 - $180,000.

Apply now through our online application form -
https://www.netyourjob.com.au/jobs/17765.php

Sponsorship may be available to the right candidate.
